          "description": "Upward advective flux of the scalar q through the velocity faces z𝑤: the air mass flux fρ times q interpolated linearly to the face (centred). This is the Fortran scalar flux (fa_zc_plumerise) in the limit of vanishing time step, in which its Lax-Wendroff-type correction (proportional to Δt) vanishes and its positivity limiter (which acts only when a face would remove half of a cell in one step) never acts. The lowest face coincides with the lower-boundary level, so its value is q[1]; the top face carries no flux. Flux units: kg m⁻² s⁻¹ times the units of q."
