        {
          "id": "williams_flats_maritime",
          "description": "The same fire with the maritime Berry autoconversion of the Fortran (droplet number 50 per cm3, dispersion 0.366), so that rain forms in the cloud, partly freezes and grows ice by deposition: cloud water, rain and ice through the cloud at 1200 s, with the plume top and two velocities. Reference: the stand-alone Fortran (tartanrunner25/Plume-model_stand_alone at 9265514, GNU Fortran 11.5.0 -O3) with the Williams Flats inputs, built with the corrections listed as departures (1)-(4) and (7)-(10) (preprocessor flags FIX_PR FIX_SED FIX_SUBL FIX_LEAPFROG), its maximum time step reduced from 5 s to 0.2 s (DTMAX) and its sponge time fixed at 15 s (FIXED_SPONGE), so that it approximates the continuous-time limit this model represents; values are interpolated linearly in time between the two Fortran steps that bracket the assertion time and converted to the state units (temperature excess T - Te, water in g/kg, tracer as a fraction of the boundary value 1000). Tolerances are about twice the largest model-reference difference measured for each field over the asserted levels (one tolerance per field and test), with floors of 0.2 % (relative), 0.02 K and one grid level (100 m) for hp. Levels at the advancing plume head, where the reference itself changes by several per cent between 0.2 s and 0.1 s steps, are not asserted.",
